Package: libheif-plugin-hwdec
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${hwdec:libheif}, ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: va-driver-all | va-driver
Suggests: intel-media-va-driver-non-free
Enhances: libheif1
Description: GPU-accelerated HEVC and AV1 decoder plugin for libheif
 Decodes HEIC (HEVC) and AVIF (AV1) images on the GPU through FFmpeg's
 hardware acceleration API, using VAAPI (Intel, AMD, and NVIDIA with
 nvidia-vaapi-driver), CUDA/NVDEC (NVIDIA) or Vulkan Video. Every program that
 reads HEIC or AVIF files through libheif uses it once the package is
 installed, including image viewers that use KDE's Qt image format plugins,
 such as Gwenview.
 .
 When no suitable GPU is present the plugin steps aside and libheif keeps
 using its usual HEVC decoder. Streams the GPU cannot decode are decoded in
 software by FFmpeg.
